      "content": "2.5 Rivers"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "epg2a7d",
      "content": "Uttarakhand is the source of two of India's most sacred rivers — the Ganga and Yamuna — and is thus called 'Devbhoomi' (Land of Gods). The state is drained by two main river systems: Ganga system and Yamuna system."
    },
